{"kind":"request","text":"Design note: platform rules that replay needs (K1 and K6 of docs/kernel.md). Item 3 of request ea7e2aa6 folds into this note.\n\nK1: a platform scope pins platform:\u003cname\u003e@\u003cn\u003e, and replay derives it only with code that its caller supplies. K6: replay names platform versions and lanes, so a second verifier would have to copy them. The note chooses one of the three ways that docs/kernel.md section 5 gives for K1 to pass (pin each version's rules by digest and archive the code; move the shipped versions into a frozen part of the kernel; or replace the marks with declared forms), says why, and says how K6's names move into platform data that the verifier reads.\n\nInput: an inventory of which deployed scopes pin or use each version and each older form. Name at least application install v1, standing destination versions 5 and 6, the archive target's legacy mode, the legacy receiver reads and the legacy MCP session revision. The deployed cohorts are in 99d86feb; the rooms on artroom-scope are still to be read. The receiver read mode and the MCP session revision are client forms, not pins, so the note measures their use separately.\n\nKernel promise 2 holds: every entry form ever written stays replayable. Code that a recorded entry needs, hosted, archived or in a fixture, moves to the archived path and is never deleted. The note deletes code only where it shows that no recorded entry needs it.\n\nThe note lists the builder slices in order and files none. Start after F3 (8fda2549) lands.","body":{"conditions":"Document only: one design note under notes/ with a status line, and docs/kernel.md and docs/roadmap.md updated when it lands. Plain English per ISO 24495-1 for a technical audience; no product names other than GitHub. Checker review before landing; land after approval.","priority":"start after F3 (8fda2549) lands","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}